That I in thy abundance am sufficed,
And dost him grace when clouds do stint their show'rs,
Within be fed, without be rich no more:
So then thou hast not lost the dues of one;
If all the year were playing holiday,
Art thou to thy fair summer but a fly,
And makest waste in limits far exceeding;
Shall rise from thee, fair tricks of white and red;
And makest waste in limits far exceeding;
Spend'st thou thy heaviness within a mile,
Looking on darkness which the blind do see:
